    "type": "question",
    "label": "78",
    "prompt": "Let $f$ and $g$ be functions such that $f(g(x))=x$. Show that $g'(x)=\\dfrac{1}{f'(g(x))}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$g'(x)=\\dfrac{1}{f'(g(x))}$.\n\nDifferentiate $f(g(x))=x$ by the chain rule, then solve for $g'(x)$.",
      "worked": "Differentiate both sides of $f(g(x))=x$:\n$$\\begin{align*}f'(g(x))g'(x)&=1\\\\g'(x)&=\\frac{1}{f'(g(x))}.\\end{align*}$$",
